WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:16.110
Last time: data, and keeping it private

3
00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:24.720
Chapter 5 · Capstone: Design Your Dream App

4
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:36.980
Capstone = your big, final project

5
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:47.770
You're the designer! No coding needed

6
00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:54.940
Meet Kabir, Class 4

7
00:00:54.940 --> 00:01:07.140
Kabir keeps forgetting things!

8
00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:16.010
"Kabir, where's your maths book?"

9
00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:24.040
What app would help Kabir? Think!

10
00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:33.970
Idea: Bag Buddy! Let's design it.

11
00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:37.060
Four steps to design an app

12
00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:48.810
Problem → Plan → 2 screens → 1-minute pitch

13
00:01:48.810 --> 00:02:01.490
Step 1: Help a Class 3–5 child

14
00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:13.980
Homework? Bag? Spellings? Water?

15
00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:19.930
Give it a fun name: Bag Buddy, Spell Star

16
00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:31.510
Step 2: Who? What goes in? What comes out?

17
00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:39.350
User: the person who uses the app

18
00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:48.980
Tiffin Timer: who is the user?

19
00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:53.320
The user is a school child!

20
00:02:53.320 --> 00:03:03.650
Input: what the user gives the app

21
00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:14.030
Output: what the app shows back

22
00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:25.210
Child types a word: input or output?

23
00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:33.770
Input! The star shown back is the output.

24
00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:45.830
Bus Buddy: what's the output?

25
00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:53.990
Output: the bus arrival time!

26
00:03:53.990 --> 00:04:04.320
Step 3: Draw 2 screens

27
00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:14.400
Screen 1: input · tap the subjects

28
00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:22.040
Screen 2: output · the checklist

29
00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:30.870
Paper and pencil. No coding needed!

30
00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:36.640
Add one idea from earlier chapters

31
00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:47.300
Variable: a box holding a changing number

32
00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:56.580
Loop: a reminder every evening

33
00:04:56.580 --> 00:05:04.590
Safety rule: never ask for a home address

34
00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:32.060
Which app idea is the clearest?

35
00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:42.420
D! Clear user, input, and output

36
00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:49.340
Step 4: a one-minute pitch

37
00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:58.320
Name · User · Input · Output · Screens

38
00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:05.330
One reason it helps. Then take a bow!

39
00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:08.260
Your turn: capstone challenge

40
00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:23.310
Write: name, user, one input, one output

41
00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:40.110
Spell Star · Class 3 · types a word → a star

42
00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:45.060
Your app helps a Class 3–5 child

43
00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:49.400
Plan: name · user · input · output

44
00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:52.970
Draw 2 screens · no coding

45
00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:59.940
1-minute pitch + one earlier idea

46
00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:11.600
All 4 units: done!

47
00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:19.600
Computer Science track complete!

48
00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:24.890
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
